WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.059
MILES WARD: Hi.

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:05.400
My name's Miles Ward.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.965
I run solutions architecture
here on Google Cloud.

00:00:07.965 --> 00:00:09.930
But this isn't my first cloud.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.380
I made the switch 3 and
1/2 years ago from AWS,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.110
and I've been talking to a
lot of customers and partners

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.420
that are in the middle of
trying to do the same thing.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.150
See, they learned the
basics about public cloud

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.120
from AWS's training and
certification programs,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.640
but they're looking at the
features of Google Cloud

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.830
and the sophistication
of our technology

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.790
and really eager to apply
that to their problems.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.560
So we thought maybe
we should put together

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.080
a training course that
leverages that existing

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.770
expertise, your familiarity
with AWS's public cloud,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.340
and allows you to apply
that to our new generation

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.510
technologies.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.850
Maybe you want to learn
more about a system that

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.400
allows you to automatically
scale from no connections

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.980
to a million connections
in under a second,

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.620
or a system that can
process petabytes of logs

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.000
without ever having
to manage an instance.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.720
Maybe you want a system that
doesn't quite cost so much.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.290
We're about 60%
cheaper on average.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.280
Or maybe you're just
tired of complexity,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.910
and you want a cloud
that is easy, easy, easy.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.110
This training course is
designed just for you.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.270
It's about six hours long.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.290
The first hour and a half covers
the fundamental differences,

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.520
the design differences,
between our cloud

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.950
and Amazon's, helps
you understand

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.020
and maybe be able
to better guess

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.900
how our system helps you
build the tools you're

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:25.770
trying to build.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.040
And then 4 and 1/2 hours
of fast-paced, deep,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.950
hands-on labs that give you
firsthand experience with

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.130
our infrastructure-as-a-service
systems but also our platform

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.140
as a service,
database as a service,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.970
both relational
and non-relational,

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.000
functions as a service, all
manner of tools that make this

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.160
such a rich suite.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.250
We think that this course
enables you not only to take

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.530
on your first experiments
with Google Cloud,

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:52.830
but prepares you in the right
way for future endeavors

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.180
and exploration.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.745
I'm excited about this course.

00:01:55.745 --> 00:01:56.370
I just took it.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.930
I thought it was
really informational.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.804
And I think you'll have
a great time with it.

00:01:59.804 --> 00:02:01.700
Thank you so much.

